TYPES.md §12.1, §8.3: a `check` written in a variant body outside any case is read like a variant-level method, `self` the variant value typed `V`: a condition that is not Bool is E3002, a case field read on `self` is E3003; and a bare call in a case body finds the variant-level method when the case has none of that name (its Int result is E3002 where a String is expected).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local variant Reward {
  item {
    count: Int

    fn text(self) -> String { return worth() }
  }
  nothing

  fn worth(self) -> Int { return 1 }

  check 1 else "not a condition"
  check self.count > 0 else "no count on the variant"
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E3002]  a/a.canon:7:38
  expected String, found Int

error[E3002]  a/a.canon:13:9
  expected Bool, found Int

error[E3003]  a/a.canon:14:14
  a.Reward has no field count

3 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
